1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. g3 d6 4. d4 Bg7 5. Bg2 O-O 6. O-O c6 7. Nc3 Re8 8. h3
Be6 9. d5 cxd5 10. cxd5 Bd7 11. Be3 Na6 12. Qd2 Nc7 13. Rfd1 Nb5 14. Nxb5 Bxb5
15. Rac1 a6 16. Nd4 Bd7 17. Qb4 Rb8 18. Kh2 Bc8 19. Qc3 {(It is not clear why
White did not play 19 Nc6.)} Nd7 20. Qc7 Qxc7 21. Rxc7 Nc5 22. b4 Na4 23. Rdc1
Kf8 24. Be4 Rd8 25. Bc2 Nb6 26. Bb3 Rd7 27. R7c2 Rd8 28. Ne6+ Bxe6 29. Bxb6 Bf5
30. Bxd8 Bxc2 31. Bc7 Rc8 32. Rxc2 {Sources: Cheltenham Chronicle, 13 August
1927 (The columnist, W S Branch, noted that White did not play 19 Nc6 and at
the end of the game wrote: 'Not so well played by the winner as we expected to
find it. Perhaps not one of her best games in the tourney.'); Staffordshire
Advertiser, 13 August 1927} 1-0

